  "articleBody": "It's super frustrating when you paint your bathroom, only to see it peeling or bubbling just a few months later. Oftentimes, this happens because bathrooms are unique spaces with a lot of moisture and temperature fluctuations. If you're not using the right paint type, or if the surface isn't prepped correctly, that fresh coat won't stand a chance. We see this a lot when folks try to cut corners, but it really makes a difference to clean walls thoroughly, address any mildew, and repair cracks before even thinking about paint. Skipping these steps is a major cause of paint failure in bathrooms, as is rushing the drying process between coats. Your bathroom needs a little extra love because of its damp environment, so proper prep and suitable materials are key to a lasting finish. If you're consistently battling peeling paint or notice significant mildew, it might be time to bring in a professional for a more durable solution.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}